    "summary": "A woman&#039;s calf-length shirt / chemise; long-sleeved, part of festive attire.  Ground made of beige tabby woven cotton cloth (muslin) with natural cream seersucker stripes.  Four full weaving widths of 36.5 cms used, to give a straight garment; hand stitched.   Long, vertical centre front opening to below bustline.  Decorated with cream and black crocheted trim using silk yarns.  Wide, straight sleeves, decorated at ends with blocks of cream and dark blue crocheted silk thread trim.",
